The timeout is caused by the complexity of the double-buffering implementation with `if/else` branches on `cur_buf`, complete array partitioning of large 2D arrays, and deeply nested structures. I'll simplify by reverting to a clean, straightforward structure that keeps the essential double-buffering concept but uses a simple `ping` flag and reduces aggressive partitioning.

```cpp
#include "mvt.h"
#include <string.h>

#ifndef TILE
#define TILE 32
#endif

extern "C" {

void kernel_mvt(
		double x1[ N + 0],
		double x2[ N + 0],
		double y_1[ N + 0],
		double y_2[ N + 0],
		double A[ N + 0][N + 0])
{
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=x1  offset=slave bundle=gmem0
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=x2  offset=slave bundle=gmem1
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=y_1 offset=slave bundle=gmem2
#pragma HLS INTERFACE m_axi port=y_2 offset=slave bundle=gmem3
